  "reasoning": "The product is a substituted uracil derivative containing a biaryl linkage between a phenyl ring and a brominated pyrimidine ring. Given the explicit context of C-C bond formation, the retrosynthetic strategy focuses on a Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling at this biaryl junction. Disconnecting this C-C bond assigns a boronic acid functionality to the phenyl partner and retains the bromine halide on the pyrimidine partner. The phenyl precursor is thus p-aminophenylboronic acid (Nc1ccc(B(O)O)cc1), matching the amide-bearing aryl fragment. The heterocyclic precursor is 2-amino-4-bromopyrimidine (Nc1nc(Br)cnc1), preserving the bromine required for the coupling. These two units align with the standard reactant patterns for C-C bond formation seen in the reference set.",
  "final_answer": "Nc1ccc(B(O)O)cc1.Nc1nc(Br)cnc1"
}

